<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Jiancheng</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jiancheng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Jiancheng was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, and the designated crown prince. Rivalry with his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> ended in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanwu-gate-incident">Xuanwu Gate Incident</a> of 626, in which Li Jiancheng was killed. Li Shimin then became emperor as Taizong.</p></div>
